{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1069", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Subject: Invitation to Meeting on Current Project Status\n\nDear Team Members\n\nI am writing to inform you that a meeting has been scheduled to discuss the current status of our ongoing project. The meeting will take place on Friday at 2 PM in the conference room on the second floor of our headquarters building.\n\nAs you are aware our project involves multiple stakeholders and various tasks that are highly correlated with each other. It is essential that we all are on the same page regarding the progress made so far and the challenges that lie ahead.\n\nDuring the meeting we will be reviewing the project timeline and assessing the current state of our deliverables. We will also be discussing the issues that the team is experiencing with regards to resource allocation and task prioritization.\n\nThe meeting will be led by our project manager who will be presenting an update on the project's overall status. The presentation will include key highlights and lowlights as well as a detailed analysis of the project's budget and expenditure.\n\nWe will also be having a Q&A session where team members can raise any concerns or questions they may have regarding the project. This is an excellent opportunity for everyone to get clarity on any doubts they may be having and to get a better understanding of how their tasks fit into the larger project landscape.\n\nIn preparation for the meeting I request that you all review the project documentation and familiarize yourselves with the current project status. You can access the relevant documents on our shared drive or by clicking on this link.\n\nIt is essential that we all come prepared to the meeting with any questions or concerns we may have. We will be taking minutes during the meeting so that we can follow up on any action items that are assigned to team members.\n\nThe agenda for the meeting is a